# Third-party software in the variPEPS extension modules

The extension modules of variPEPS (GPL-3.0-or-later) contain code of the
following projects, compiled from source when the package is built. Their
license texts, with the copyright notices, conditions and disclaimers, are in
the subdirectories next to this file.

| Project | Version | License | Used in |
|---|---|---|---|
| tblis (https://github.com/MatthewsResearchGroup/tblis) | commit @TBLIS_COMMIT@ | BSD-3-Clause, `tblis/LICENSE` | `_tblis_contract` (static) |
| marray, stl_ext, TCI (bundled with tblis) | as in tblis | BSD-3-Clause, `marray/`, `stl_ext/`, `tci/` | `_tblis_contract` (static) |
| BLIS (https://github.com/flame/blis) | commit @BLIS_GIT_TAG@ | BSD-3-Clause, `blis/LICENSE` | `_tblis_contract` (static) |
| TAPP reference implementation, API headers (https://github.com/TAPPorg/reference-implementation) | commit @TAPP_COMMIT@ | BSD-3-Clause, `tapp/LICENSE.md` | `_tblis_contract` (headers) |
| nanobind (https://github.com/wjakob/nanobind) | @NANOBIND_VERSION@ | BSD-3-Clause, `nanobind/LICENSE` | `_tblis_contract`, `_svd_only_u_vt` (static) |

Copyright holders named in the source files in addition to the license files:

- tblis: The University of Texas at Austin, Southern Methodist University (files
  derived from BLIS).
- BLIS: The University of Texas at Austin, Advanced Micro Devices, Inc., Southern
  Methodist University, SiFive, Inc., The University of Tokyo, Hewlett Packard
  Enterprise Development LP, IBM Corp., Forschungszentrum Juelich, Linaro Limited,
  Tactical Computing Laboratories, LLC, Oracle Labs, Oracle Corporation, Devin
  Matthews, Field G. Van Zee, Dave Love (University of Manchester). Each of these
  files carries the same BSD-3-Clause license as `blis/LICENSE`.
- TAPP: the contributors listed in `tapp/AUTHORS.md`.

On Linux, `_tblis_contract` is linked dynamically against the GCC runtime
libraries libgomp, libatomic, libstdc++ and libgcc_s (GPL-3.0 with the GCC
Runtime Library Exception; the GPL-3.0 text is the license of variPEPS itself,
the exception is in `gcc_runtime/`). The wheels on PyPI contain copies of
libgomp and libatomic (bundled by `auditwheel repair`); libstdc++ and libgcc_s
are taken from the system. The macOS build links none of them (no OpenMP), only
the system libraries of macOS (libc++, libSystem).
